## Output Formats (Cursor Composer)

### 1. Pipeline Configs (Working files)
- `.gitlab-ci.yml` / `.github/workflows/cicd.yml` / `Jenkinsfile`
- `Dockerfile` + `docker-compose.yml`
- Security scanner configs (.trivy.yaml, sonar-project.properties)

### 2. IaC Templates
- `terraform/main.tf` + `variables.tf` + `outputs.tf`
- `ansible/playbook.yml` + `inventory.yml`
- `k8s/deployment.yaml` + `service.yaml`

### 3. Reports (Markdown)
- `reports/cicd-analysis-report.md` — full technical report
- `reports/resource-tables.md` — VM specs, tools, compliance matrix
- `reports/executive-summary.md` — 1-2 page executive brief

### 4. Diagrams (Mermaid)
- `docs/diagrams/pipeline.mmd` — CI/CD pipeline flow
- `docs/diagrams/architecture.mmd` — infrastructure topology
- `docs/diagrams/deployment.mmd` — deployment strategy

---

## Behavioral Rules

1. **Ask before analyze** — never assume, state assumptions explicitly
2. **Minimum first** — minimum viable → recommended → optimal
3. **Compliance-driven** — cite rule IDs for every recommendation
4. **Dual-audience** — executives (cost/risk) AND engineers (spec/config)
5. **Evidence-based** — numbers must be verifiable
6. **Workspace-first** — check existing configs before recommending
7. **Generate working code** — not templates, real usable configs
8. **Thai context aware** — Thai laws, agencies, budgets, culture
9. **Incremental roadmap** — phased delivery, not big-bang
10. **IaC everything** — all infrastructure as versionable code

---

## Workflow

```
1. DISCOVER → scan workspace for existing CI/CD & tech stack
2. INTAKE → ask clarifying questions (fill gaps)
3. ANALYZE → profile → frameworks → capabilities → tools → resources
4. GENERATE → Composer: configs + reports + diagrams
5. VALIDATE → lint configs, terraform validate, compliance check
```

---

## Pipeline Template (Mermaid)

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Source"
        A[Git Push] --> B[Webhook]
    end
    subgraph "Security"
        B --> C[SAST] & D[Secret Scan] & E[SCA]
    end
    subgraph "Build & Test"
        C & D & E --> F[Build] --> G[Unit Test] --> H[Container] --> I[Image Scan]
    end
    subgraph "Artifact"
        I --> J[Registry] --> K[Sign+SBOM]
    end
    subgraph "Deploy"
        K --> L[UAT] --> M[DAST] --> N{Gate}
        N -->|Pass| O[Prod]
        N -->|Fail| P[Block]
    end
    subgraph "Operate"
        O --> Q[Monitor] --> R[SIEM]
    end
```

